&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The AI Teams at Agile Robots&lt;/strong&gt; are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Machine Learning Engineer (m/f/d) VLA Training &amp;amp; Evaluation&lt;/strong&gt;, who will build the frameworks for fine-tuning and benchmarking robot foundation models on collected robot data. The frameworks are meant to work across different foundation models and for teams with modest data and compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training Workflows:&lt;/strong&gt; Build reusable, model-agnostic training and evaluation workflows, with experiment tracking, model versioning, and checkpoint management, so that different foundation models can be swapped in without rebuilding the pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fine-Tuning:&lt;/strong&gt; Implement fine-tuning of pretrained vision-language-action models on collected robot data, for example with parameter-efficient methods such as LoRA or adapters, or with distillation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Policy Training:&lt;/strong&gt; Build training loops for action-chunking and transformer-based action models, diffusion policies, and VLM/VLA heads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benchmarks:&lt;/strong&gt; Build benchmarks with generalization splits, success metrics, and failure-analysis templates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transfer Studies:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with simulation engineers on studies, including metrics and ablations, that test whether improvements in simulation realism improve performance on the real robot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research Baselines:&lt;/strong&gt; Turn published methods into working baselines and templates that others can extend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Academic Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Degree in Computer Science, Machine Learning, Robotics, or a related field (Master’s or PhD typical), or an equivalent combination of formal training and demonstrated experience training deep learning models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training Internals:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience writing and debugging training loops in PyTorch or JAX, including data loading, loss design, and optimizer behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fine-Tuning:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience fine-tuning pretrained models and adapting them to new tasks and data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Robot Learning:&lt;/strong&gt; Working understanding of how imitation-learned policies, such as action-chunking or diffusion policies, turn observations into robot actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experiment Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience designing evaluations and ablations, and running experiments with tracking, versioning, and checkpoint management so that others can reproduce them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneficial Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;VLA Models:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience fine-tuning vision-language-action or vision-language models for robot control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real-Robot Evaluation:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience evaluating learned policies on physical robots.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sim-to-Real:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with measuring how well models trained in simulation transfer to real hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;TranslationField-module__fieldItemName___Q0F_7 TranslationField-module__aboutUsWrapper___WXJpq&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
